  "body": {
    "id": "lem:four-line-classification",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "In the specialization \\(N=3,r=s=1\\) and \\(\\gamma=\\kappa_\\star=1/\\sqrt3\\), the maximal-margin loading class is exactly \\(\\{\\operatorname{range}(P_h):h\\in\\mathcal H_4\\}\\). Distinct projectors satisfy \\(\\lVert P_h-P_{h'}\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}=2\\sqrt2/3\\). For the four-hypothesis Gaussian experiment \\(\\mathcal E_4(T_0)\\), with nuisance parameters \\(d,f,\\sigma\\) profiled over their full stated sets, the nearest-projector rule obeys \\(\\max_{h\\in\\mathcal H_4}\\sup_{d,f,\\sigma}\\mathbb P_{h,d,f,\\sigma}(\\widehat h\\ne h)\\le p_{\\mathrm{cls}}(T_0)=\\min\\{1,18V_0/(T_0d_{\\mathrm{lo}}^4)\\}\\). Hence \\(T_0\\ge\\overline T\\) implies uniform misclassification probability at most \\(\\alpha/2\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "N",
      "r",
      "s",
      "T0",
      "alpha",
      "dlo",
      "sigma",
      "kappaStar",
      "gamma",
      "V0",
      "H4",
      "Ph",
      "E4",
      "hhat",
      "pcls",
      "Tbar"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:model-class",
      "def:four-line-experiment",
      "lem:pre-projector-region"
    ],
    "justification": "The explicit profiled experiment turns the endpoint geometry into a uniform finite-sample decision bound with a declared error budget.",
    "gap": "EvansHansenStark2005 supplies abstract confidence-set decision duality but does not identify these four Gaussian components or profile the panel nuisances \\(d,f,\\sigma\\).",
    "consumer": "It certifies when a loading-margin oracle may spend part of its noncoverage budget on component classification without widening the reported effect set.",
    "proof_tex": "In the specialization \\(N=3,r=s=1\\), write \\(L=\\operatorname{span}(u)\\) with \\(\\lVert u\\rVert_2=1\\).  For a two-element set \\(S\\) with complementary index \\(i\\),\n\\[\nE_S^{\\top}(I_3-uu^{\\top})E_S=I_2-u_Su_S^{\\top},\n\\]\nwhose least eigenvalue is \\(1-\\lVert u_S\\rVert_2^2=u_i^2\\).  Hence\n\\[\n\\kappa_1(L)=\\min_{1\\le i\\le3}|u_i|le {1\\over\\sqrt3},\n\\]\nwith equality if and only if \\(|u_1|=|u_2|=|u_3|=1/\\sqrt3\\).  After quotienting by the irrelevant global sign, these are exactly the four lines indexed by \\(h\\in\\mathcal H_4\\), so \\(\\kappa_\\star=1/\\sqrt3\\).\n\nIf \\(h\\ne h'\\) index distinct lines, then \\(|u_h^{\\top}u_{h'}|=1/3\\).  For rank-one projectors the nonzero principal angle gives\n\\[\n\\lVert P_h-P_{h'}\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\n=\\sqrt{1-(u_h^{\\top}u_{h'})^2}={2\\sqrt2\\over3}.\n\\]\nFix the true label \\(h\\).  If \\(\\widehat h\\ne h\\), the nearest-projector rule and the triangle inequality imply\n\\[\n{2\\sqrt2\\over3}\n\\le\\lVert P_h-P_{\\widehat h}\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\n\\le\\lVert P_h-\\widehat P\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\n  +\\lVert\\widehat P-P_{\\widehat h}\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\n\\le2\\lVert\\widehat P-P_h\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}.\n\\]\nThus misclassification implies \\(e^2\\ge2/9\\).  The squared projector bound already proved is uniform over every profiled \\(d,f,\\sigma\\) in \\(\\mathcal E_4(T_0)\\), and Markov's inequality yields\n\\[\n\\sup_{d,f,\\sigma}\\Pr_{h,d,f,\\sigma}(\\widehat h\\ne h)\n\\le {9\\over2}\\,{4V_0\\over T_0d_{\\mathrm{lo}}^4}\n={18V_0\\over T_0d_{\\mathrm{lo}}^4}.\n\\]\nTaking the minimum with one gives \\(p_{\\mathrm{cls}}(T_0)\\).  If \\(T_0\\ge\\overline T\\), the definition of \\(\\overline T\\) gives \\(18V_0/(T_0d_{\\mathrm{lo}}^4)\\le\\alpha/2\\), completing the proof.",
